    "culture": {
      "text": {
        "id": 42,
        "title": "NFL legend John Madden’s unlikely, unfiltered brilliance: ‘Coach was indeed animated’",
        "source": "The Guardian - Culture",
        "source_id": "guardian_culture",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/nov/20/john-madden-nfl-football-biopic",
        "published_at": "2026-11-20T10:00:31",
        "level": "B1",
        "slot_level": "B1",
        "source_level": "B2",
        "word_count": 2257,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "Wearing his Oakland Raiders uniform and helmet, and gripping an orange traffic cone like a lance, Ted Hendricks rode into the training session on a roan horse and stopped at the 50-yard line. Some American football coaches might have reacted to the stunt with fury. But John Madden was unfazed.",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "399046e2c9f5a6b88f26aec224b7f9f801efca53",
        "summary": "With the release of a new David O Russell biopic about the coach turned commentator turned gaming icon, those who knew him best remember his singular career Wearing his Oakland Raiders uniform and helmet, and gripping an orange traffic cone like a lance, Ted Hendricks rode into the training session on a roan horse and stopped at the 50-yard line. Some American football coaches might have reacted to the stunt with fury. But John Madden was unfazed. “We needed some relief from the intense grind,” recalls Hendricks, 79, who had borrowed the horse from a nearby stable. “It was a spur of the moment idea, but put a smile on everyone’s face. All Coach said once I dismounted was, ‘All right guys, Ted’s here, let’s get started.’ But I know he got a kick out of it too – just from the look on his face and the comments he made later in interviews.”",
        "origin": "adjacent",
        "badges": [
          "Closest level: B2",
          "Outside preferred window"
        ],
